--- STEP 1: SURVEY — shared SSE taxonomy + web live hooks ------------
Shared KMP core (apps/shared/core/.../net/sse):
  SseClient.subscribe(path) -> LiveSubscription(
      events: Flow<LiveEvent>,
      connection: StateFlow<Connection>)
  Connection (enum): Connecting, Open, Reconnecting, Stale, Closed
    - 2-minute freshness window (ADR-013); Stale never drops the stream.
    - auto-reconnect: capped exponential backoff + jitter, resumes Last-Event-ID.
  LiveEvent (sealed): Connected(clientId), Heartbeat(time), VehicleUpdate(json),
    Alert(json), ExportStatus(json), AchievementUnlocked(json),
    Signal(SignalEnvelope{vehicleId,field,kind,value,ts}), Unknown(event,data).
  SseConfig.freshnessWindowMillis = 120_000 (the 2-min stale contract).

Swift facade already present (Sources/SharedFacade):
  LiveConnectionState (connecting/open/reconnecting/stale/closed, hasUsableData),
  LiveEventKind (connected/heartbeat/vehicleUpdate/alert/exportStatus/
    achievementUnlocked/signal/unknown), LiveEvent (id, kind, raw:SharedLiveEvent),
  FlowBridge.stream(from:) — Kotlin Flow -> AsyncThrowingStream (cancel-safe).
  AuthChallengeHandling.handleUnauthorized() — single-flight 401 refresh (P5).
  AuthTokenProviding.validAccessToken() — refresh-if-expiring (P5).

Web hooks surveyed (web/src):
  hooks/useRealtimeEvents.ts  — singleton SSE pipe; states connected|reconnecting;
                                 callbacks vehicle_update/alert/export_status/
                                 achievement_unlocked/connected/disconnected.
  hooks/useLiveConnection.ts  — status connected|reconnecting|disconnected|unknown;
                                 lastMessageAt; 10s reconnecting grace -> disconnected.
  features/telemetry/hooks/useLiveSignalStream.ts — per-page signal subscription
                                 (chart + tail) over the one shared pipe; 5-min
                                 rolling window; vehicle-scoped filter.

DESIGN DECISIONS (mirrors web + ADR-009/013):
  * Foreground-only: connect only when scene .active AND a subscribing view is
    visible; deactivate on background/disappear. SSE is NEVER a background
    notification channel (APNs is P6-0002).
  * Resume: store remembers Last-Event-ID and passes it on re-subscribe across
    foreground cycles; within a subscription the shared client resumes itself.
  * Staleness: store derives stale = (now - lastActivity) > 120s OR phase==.stale.
  * Auth: 401 -> AuthChallengeHandling.handleUnauthorized() -> retry once per
    activation; second consecutive auth failure surfaces error (coordinator
    drives reauthRequired). Token is read fresh on each (re)connect.
  * Seam is closure-based + Shared-free (LiveStreamProvider<Event>) so tests use
    a scripted AsyncStream with no KMP objects; production adapter wraps SseClient.

